"Rep. Vargas, Juan","party":"D","state":"CA"},"stage":"passed_origin","stage_label":"Passed one chamber","summary":null,"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Credit Union Board Modernization Act","viability":70.9,"viability_status":"active"},"date":"2025-02-11","detail":"Related bill","id":"119-hr-975","label":"H.R. 975","title":"Credit Union Board Modernization Act","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/975"}]},"selection":{"reason":"Impact scored and summarised by Gemini.","status":"analyzed"},"sources":{"latest":{"date":"2026-07-22","label":"Referred in Senate","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr6955/BILLS-119hr6955rfs.htm"},"other":[{"label":"This bill on Congress.gov","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/6955"}],"past":[{"date":"2026-07-21","label":"Engrossed in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr6955/BILLS-119hr6955eh.htm"},{"date":"2026-04-20","label":"Reported in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr6955/BILLS-119hr6955rh.htm"},{"date":"2026-01-07","label":"Introduced in House","url":"https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr6955/BILLS-119hr6955ih.htm"}]},"sponsor":{"chamber":"House","district":"2","id":"H001072","name":"Rep. Hill, J. French","party":"R","state":"AR"},"stage":"passed_origin","stage_label":"Passed one chamber","summary":"The Main Street Capital Access Act modifies and lessens various banking regulations, adjusts capitalization requirements and asset thresholds for community banks and holding companies, and alters federal bank supervision, merger reviews, and resolution procedures.","summary_detail":{"affected_groups":[{"effect":"Receive regulatory relief, reduced capital and leverage requirements, higher asset thresholds, and streamlined examination processes.","group":"Community Banks and Small Bank Holding Companies"},{"effect":"Subject to new reporting requirements, mandatory reviews of guidance and regulations, strict deadlines for application approvals, and oversight by an independent review board.","group":"Federal Financial Regulators"},{"effect":"Benefit from clearer timelines, deemed-approved provisions for delayed applications, and exemptions from specific antitrust reviews for transactions under $10 billion.","group":"Financial Institutions Engaging in Mergers"}],"key_provisions":["Provides a three-year capital requirement phase-in period for new banks and reduces the leverage ratio for certain rural community banks.","Requires financial regulators to tailor rules based on risk profiles and business models, and periodically index thresholds to economic indicators.","Establishes an Office of Independent Examination Review and gives financial institutions the right to an independent review of material supervisory determinations.","Eases bank merger requirements by exempting certain transactions under $10 billion from specific monopoly and competition considerations, and sets application processing deadlines.","Modifies the Least Cost Resolution exception to allow alternative resolution methods under certain conditions to limit banking concentration in global systemically important institutions.","Extends the permitted holding period for merchant banking investments to at least 15 years."],"missing_information":["The exact long-term fiscal impact on the Deposit Insurance Fund resulting from the new Least Cost Resolution exception is not fully determined.","The specific economic indicators and final threshold values to be selected by the Board of Governors for future regulatory adjustments are not predetermined."],"plain_summary":"The Main Street Capital Access Act modifies and lessens various banking regulations, adjusts capitalization requirements and asset thresholds for community banks and holding companies, and alters federal bank supervision, merger reviews, and resolution procedures.","significance":"The legislation alters the regulatory framework governing U.S. banks and credit unions by reducing compliance burdens for smaller institutions, altering supervisory appeals processes, and changing how federal regulators review bank mergers and failures."},"summary_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-25T21:32:49+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text+summary","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr6955/BILLS-119hr6955rfs.htm"]},"summary_threshold":50,"title":"Main Street Capital Access Act","viability":69.1,"viability_detail":{"breakdown":[{"available":true,"effective_weight":35.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Detected stage","value":"Passed one chamber"}],"key":"stage","label":"Legislative stage","note":"Stage value from the table on the About page.","points":28.0,"value":0.8,"weight":35},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Committee activity","value":"Reported out of committee (or past committee stage)"}],"key":"committee","label":"Committee activity","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Floor activity","value":"Passed a chamber"}],"key":"floor","label":"Floor consideration","note":"","points":15.0,"value":1.0,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":15.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Days since latest action","value":95},{"label":"Half-life (days)","value":90}],"key":"momentum","label":"Recent action","note":"","points":7.22,"value":0.4811,"weight":15},{"available":true,"effective_weight":10.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Cosponsors","value":33},{"label":"House majority","value":218}],"key":"cosponsors","label":"Cosponsorship","note":"","points":3.89,"value":0.3891,"weight":10},{"available":true,"effective_weight":10.0,"inputs":[{"label":"Democratic supporters","value":0},{"label":"Republican supporters","value":34}],"key":"bipartisan","label":"Bipartisan support","note":"Sponsor plus cosponsors; independents are not counted toward either party.","points":0.0,"value":0.0,"weight":10}],"data_completeness":1.0,"formula_version":"1.1","reached_stage":"passed_origin","s